ha-citrine source patch 0007 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27), applied after 0001 to 0006:
OCPP 2.1 charging needs that arrive before the transaction
(ha-addons#106).

With TxStartPoints PowerPathClosed, an ISO 15118-20 EV states its needs in
ScheduleExchangeReq and the station sends NotifyEVChargingNeeds before
TransactionEvent Started. Upstream answered Rejected when no transaction
existed. Under OCPP 2.1 a station treats Rejected as a refusal of the energy
transfer and ends the session (K19.FR.16; libocpp calls
stop_transaction_callback with ReqEnergyTransferRejected).

NotifyEVChargingNeeds (OCPP 2.1):
- needs with no transaction are stored on the EVSE without a transaction and
  answered NoChargingProfile (no schedule follows; the station starts at once);
- needs for an OCPP 2.1 mode or with v2xChargingParameters are stored and
  answered NoChargingProfile, with or without a transaction (patch 0001
  answered Accepted and sent no profile);
- Rejected stays for needs without usable parameters, and AC parameters no
  longer match the OCPP 2.1 DC modes (DC_BPT, DC_ACDP, DC_ACDP_BPT);
- OCPP 2.0.1 is unchanged: Rejected without a transaction, and the upstream
  profile calculation for the 2.0.1 modes with one.

TransactionEvent Started links the EVSE's pending needs from the last 10
minutes to the new transaction (a new row: transactionCreatedAt is part of
the primary key) and removes the EVSE's unlinked rows.

ChargingNeeds gains v2xChargingParameters (JSONB), controlMode and
mobilityNeedsMode (migration 20261026150000-add-charging-needs-v2x), in the
Sequelize model, the Drizzle schema and the DTO. transactionDatabaseId may be
null. Hasura selects every column already.

Tests: needs before and after the transaction, V2X and DC under OCPP 2.1, a
storage failure, mismatched parameters, OCPP 2.0.1 unchanged, and the link on
Started (not on Updated, failure tolerated).

